cells:
  - kind: 1
    value: |-
      # Test and Demo the Select AI Agent Tool RANK_STOPS_FOR_SHADE

      **HrOUG 2026 · Spatial Meets AI · Demo 3**

      Author: Karin Patenge · October 2026

      **Prerequisites**

      * Connect as the demo schema `HROUG2026`.
      * `create_tool_rank_stops_for_shade.sqlnb` has created the function, the tool and the agent team.
      * The AI profile `OCI_GENAI_PROFILE` exists (`spatial_using_select_ai.sql`, part 2).

      **Order on stage:** Select AI with the profile first (section 1), then the agent team (section 3). After `SET_TEAM`, only `SELECT AI AGENT` works in the session; `SELECT AI SHOWSQL`, `RUNSQL` or `NARRATE` fail with `ORA-20046` ("not supported for current session") until `DBMS_CLOUD_AI.SET_PROFILE` is called again (section 4).

      **No question mark at the end of a SELECT AI prompt.** The prompt is not quoted, so JDBC clients (SQLcl, SQL Developer) take `?` as a bind placeholder and fail with `ORA-17041` (missing IN or OUT parameter).

      Documentation: [Select AI Agent](https://docs.oracle.com/en-us/iaas/autonomous-database-serverless/doc/select-ai-agent1.html) · File encoding: UTF-8 (Croatian diacritics).
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: >-
      ## Table of Contents


      1. Set the AI profile for this session and ask in natural language
      (NL2SQL)

      2. Test the function behind the tool

      3. Run the agent team in this session (SELECT AI AGENT only from here on)

      4. Back to SELECT AI with the profile in the same session (clears the
      team; GET_TEAM returns NULL)
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "## 1. Set the AI profile for this session and ask in natural language
      (NL2SQL)"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: |
      BEGIN
        DBMS_CLOUD_AI.SET_PROFILE(profile_name => 'OCI_GENAI_PROFILE');
      END;
      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "SELECT AI SHOWSQL show the 10 ZET stops with the most weekday
      departures;\r\n"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## 2. Test the function behind the tool"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      -- Expected: TREES first with the largest cooling (Odvojak Reber, about
      2.6 °C),

      -- then SHELTER with the busiest heat-island stops where trees cool less
      than 1 °C

      -- (Glavni kolodvor, Trg bana J. Jelačića, Zapruđe: each merged from 2 or
      3 stations)

      SELECT rank_stops_for_shade(tree_stops => 10, shelter_stops => 5) AS
      result FROM dual;
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: |
      -- The same answer as rows
      SELECT
        r.*
      FROM
        JSON_TABLE(
          rank_stops_for_shade(tree_stops => 10, shelter_stops => 5),
          '$.recommendations[*]'
          COLUMNS (
            action              VARCHAR2(10)  PATH '$.action',
            action_rank         NUMBER        PATH '$.rank',
            stop_name           VARCHAR2(100) PATH '$.stop_name',
            stop_ids            VARCHAR2(100) PATH '$.stop_ids',
            stations            NUMBER        PATH '$.stations',
            district            VARCHAR2(100) PATH '$.district',
            vehicles            VARCHAR2(30)  PATH '$.vehicles',
            weekday_departures  NUMBER        PATH '$.weekday_departures',
            surface_temp_c      NUMBER        PATH '$.surface_temp_c',
            tree_cooling_c      NUMBER        PATH '$.tree_cooling_c',
            reason              VARCHAR2(200) PATH '$.reason'
          )
        ) r;
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      -- Merged stations: expected Glavni kolodvor once, 2 stations (109, 110),
      BUS/TRAM, 2,336 departures

      SELECT
        r.*
      FROM
        JSON_TABLE(
          rank_stops_for_shade(tree_stops => 0, shelter_stops => 100),
          '$.recommendations[*]'
          COLUMNS (
            stop_name           VARCHAR2(100) PATH '$.stop_name',
            stop_ids            VARCHAR2(100) PATH '$.stop_ids',
            stations            NUMBER        PATH '$.stations',
            vehicles            VARCHAR2(30)  PATH '$.vehicles',
            weekday_departures  NUMBER        PATH '$.weekday_departures'
          )
        ) r
      WHERE
        r.stop_name = 'Glavni kolodvor';
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      -- Filters: both Novi Zagreb districts, tram stops only (district matching
      ignores case and č, ć, ž, š, đ)

      SELECT rank_stops_for_shade(tree_stops => 3, shelter_stops => 3, district
      => 'novi zagreb', vehicle => 'tram') AS result FROM dual;
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      -- Invalid input: expected {"error":"Ask for at least one stop: ..."}

      SELECT rank_stops_for_shade(tree_stops => 0, shelter_stops => 0) AS result
      FROM dual;
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## 3. Run the agent team in this session (SELECT AI AGENT only from here
      on)"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "EXEC DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.SET_TEAM('ZG_SHADE_TEAM');\r\n"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "SELECT AI AGENT I have a budget for 20 new shelters and for planting
      trees around 10 stops. Where should they go;\r\n"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      -- In Croatian:

      SELECT AI AGENT Imam budžet za 20 novih nadstrešnica i za sadnju drveća
      oko 10 stajališta. Gdje ih postaviti;
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      -- The same from PL/SQL (also works where SELECT AI is not available, for
      example Database Actions).

      -- Here the prompt is a string literal, so a question mark is fine.

      SET SERVEROUTPUT ON
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      DECLARE
        l_answer CLOB;
      BEGIN
        l_answer := DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.RUN_TEAM(
                      team_name   => 'ZG_SHADE_TEAM',
                      user_prompt => 'I have a budget for 20 new shelters and for planting trees around 10 stops. Where should they go?');
        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(l_answer);
      END;

      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: "## 4. Back to SELECT AI with the profile in the same session (clears the
      team; GET_TEAM returns NULL)"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "EXEC DBMS_CLOUD_AI.SET_PROFILE(profile_name => 'OCI_GENAI_PROFILE');\r\n"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "SELECT DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.GET_TEAM() AS current_team FROM dual;\r\n"
    languageId: oracle-sql
